[s], pre=pre, intra=intra, post=post,\\n                             bubble=(T-busy[s])/T))\\n        agg = 1 - sum(busy)/(p*T)\\n        return dict(T=T, agg=agg, per_stage=rows, ideal=m*(self.f+self.b+self.w)/p)\\n\\n    def _dep_ready(self, k, i, u, end, p, v, m):\\n        P = p*v\\n        if k == \\\"F\\\":\\n            if i > 0 and (\\\"F\\\", i-1, u) not in end: return False  # same-unit program handled by queue\\n            return u == 0 or (\\\"F\\\", i, u-1) in end\\n        if k == \\\"B\\\":\\n            return (\\\"F\\\", i, u) in end and (u == P-1 or (\\\"B\\\", i, u+1) in end)\\n        return (\\\"B\\\", i, u) in end\\n\\n    def _dep_time(self, k, i, u, end, p, v, m):\\n        P = p*v\\n        if k == \\\"F\\\": return 0.0 if u == 0 else end[(\\\"F\\\", i, u-1)]\\n        if k == \\\"B\\\":\\n            t = end[(\\\"F\\\", i, u)]\\n            if u < P-1: t = max(t, end[(\\\"B\\\", i, u+1)])\\n            return t\\n        return end[(\\\"B\\\", i, u)]\\nPY\\necho written\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.065, \"output\": \"written\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "da397bed-d504-4a7b-9c65-20acb7f70a90", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
{"id": "ba34409b-e448-4381-ae17-1c472504946e", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:08:52.004303", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "7f2a84b8-8baf-42d2-a1d4-9dd8b482a624", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Wait: there's a bug — the \"F\" dep ready check requires (\"F\", i-1, u) done, which is wrong (forward of microbatch i on unit u doesn't depend on forward of microbatch i-1 on same unit in general... actually it does not depend, only program order). I included it as a check which is enforced by the per-device program queue anyway. Since the program queue enforces order, (\"F\", i-1,u) will be done before it's that task's turn... unless W tasks intervene. Hmm, in 1f1b order the F of microbatch i occurs after F of i-1 anyway. OK it's harmless but let me just remove for safety. Also for 1f1b the correct program order for warmup microbatches' backward: standard 1F1B does warmup F's, then steady 1F1B, then cooldown B's in FIFO order (i.e., in increasing i order, not reversed). Let me fix: cooldown in increasing order of warm_seq.\n\nLet me test against analytic formulas:\n- AFAB bubble = (p-1)/(m+p-1)\n- 1F1B bubble = (p-1)/(m+p-1) (same total idle in the balanced f=b=w?; well, with W included the \"ideal\" changes but bubble fraction formula for 1F1B with per-microbatch unit time (f+b+w)=1 and b=f: bubble = (p-1)/(m+p-1)).\n\nLet me run and see.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cd /workspace/design && sed -i 's|if i > 0 and (\"F\", i-1, u) not in end: return False  # same-unit program handled by queue\\n||' sched_sim.py && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\ns=open('/workspace/design/sched_sim.py').read()\ns=s.replace('            if i > 0 and (\"F\", i-1, u) not in end: return False  # same-unit program handled by queue\\n','')\ns=s.replace('for i in reversed(warm_seq):','for i in warm_seq:')\nopen('/workspace/design/sched_sim.py','w').write(s)\nPY\ncd /workspace/design && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom sched_sim import Sim\nprint(\"p  m 