 an honest finding to report: the naive canonical-order model with separate W does not reproduce the textbook formula, which shows why G1 must be defined carefully with an explicit convention for W (bwd = 2n or 3n convention).\n\nActually let me try one quick fix: set w=0 (no separate weight grad; b = full backward). Then check whether agg == (p-1)/(m+p-1) for 1f1b.\n\np=2,m=2,f=b=1,w=0: AFAB: stage0: F0,F1,B0,B1. deps: B(i,0) after B(i,1). T = ? F0@0-1(st0), F1@1-2(st0), F0 st1 after F0 st0 → 1-2, F1 st1 2-3, B0 st1 needs F0 → 3-4, B0 st0 needs B0 st1 → 4-5, B1 st1 needs F1(st1 3, and B2 none)→ after B0 st1 → 5-6, B1 st0 after B1 st1 → 6-7. T=7. busy per stage = 4 → agg = 1-8/14=0.4286 vs analytic (p-1)/(m+p-1)=1/3. Hmm, with m=p the classic formula's assumption m≥p... the classic 1F1B bubble = (p-1)/(m+p-1) exactly when m ≥ p... for p=2,m=2 that's 1/3. My greedy-ish earliest-time ordering yields T=7 vs predicted T = m*(f+b)*p/(p-... ) hmm: bubble ratio (p-1)/(m+p-1) means T = m(f+b)/(p-1) * ... let me recompute: for AFAB, ideal T_ideal = m*(f+b)/p... no. For p=2,m=2: total work = 2*2*2 = 8 device-time; if bubble ratio = 1/3 then T = 8/(2*(2/3)) = 6. Actual T=7 > 6 because my dependency model requires B(i,0) after B(i+1,...)? Let's see: with AFAB ordering, at stage1, after F0,F1 it does B0 then B1; stage0 does F0,F1 then B0,B1 — B0@stage0 needs B0@stage1 done (4), B1@stage0 needs B1@stage1 (6) → T=7. So T=7 and agg=4/14=0.2857? Wait I computed 1-8/14 = 0.4286. Right, 0.4286. So the standard formula assumes... The standard GPipe bubble formula is (p-1)/(m+p-1) with the assumption that the ideal per-device busy = m*(f+b) and T = (m+p-1)(f+b)/... hmm for p=2,m=2: T = (m+p-1)(f+b) = 3*2 = 6 with f+b=2. My sim gives 7. The difference: the classic derivation assumes backward at stage0 for microbatch i can start right after backward of stage1 same microbatch, with no per-device serialization conflicts... it should be fine. Let me trace the textbook: p=2,m=2. Timeline (t in units of f=1... but the formula's unit is (f+b)). Textbook says T = (m+p-1)(f+b) = 3*2 = 6. Trace: stage0: F0[0,1], F1[1,2], B0[2,3]... but B0 at stage0 requires B0 at stage1, which requires F0 at stage1 [1,2], B0 stage1 [2,3] → B0 stage0 [3,4]. stage1: F1 [3,4]? stage1 must wait for F1 from stage0 (done at 2) but is busy with B0 [2,3]; so F1 stage1 [3,4], B1 stage1 [4,5], B1 stage0 [5,6]. T=6! My sim gave 7 because AFAB ordering forced stage1 to do both forwards before any backward (that's AFAB = all-forward-all-backward, which indeed gives worse makespan than the formula). So AFAB ≠ the formula's idealization. Actually the classic formula (p-1)/(m+p-1) is for GPipe/AFAB with the assumption comm=0 and it equals... Let me recompute AFAB makespan properly: stage1 in AFAB does F0,F1 then B0,B1: F0[0,1],F1[1,2],B0[2,3],B1[3,4] where B1 needs F1 done ✓. stage0: F0[0,1],F1[1,2],B0 needs B0@stage1 done at 3 → [3,4], B1 needs B1@stage1 (4) → [4,5]. T=5, agg=1-8/10=0.2. Hmm, but my sim gave 7 — because the program order within stage1 in my model is per-unit loop... For AFAB with p=2, v=1: units u=0 (device0), u=1(device1). prog[0]=F0,F1,B0,B1,W..., prog[1]=F0,F1,B0,B1,... Then dep edges: B(0,0) <- B(0,1); B(i,1) <- F(i,1) only (u==P-1). Trace: earliest: st0 F0 0-1, F1 1-2; st1 F0 1-2, F1 2-3, B0 st1 needs F(0,1) end 2 → 3-4 (device free at 3), B1 st1 4-5, B0 st0 needs B(0,1) end 4 → 5-6, B1 st0 needs B(1,1) end 5 → 6-7. T=7. So the difference vs my manual 5 is that stage1's F1 happened at 2-3 before B0 (correct AFAB ordering) giving 3-4 for B0 — I had assumed stage1 B0 at [2,3] which is impossible since it must finish both forwards. So AFAB T=7 is right for AFAB ordering, and the textbook formula (p-1)/(m+p-1) uses \"bubble = (p-1)(f+b)\" i.e. T = m(f+b) + (p-1)(f+b) = (m+p-1)(f+b) = 6 for m=2,p=2 → that's 1-8/(2*6)=0.333 exactly the analytic. So textbook formula corresponds to an idealized schedule where comm-fill costs (p-1)(f+b), but real AFAB ordering gives (p-1)f + ... Actually real AFAB: T = m*f + (p-1)*f + m*b + (p-1)*b? For p=2,m=2: 2+1+2+... = m*f+(p-1)*f + m*b + (p-1)*b = 2+1+2+1=6? But sim says 7. Because the backward of stage1 for mb1 is delayed by its own forward of mb1 (serialization), which is real. Textbook ignores that ordering subtlety... whatever.\n\nConclusion for design purposes: exact-match G1 against the textbook formula requires a specific convention and a canonical schedule definition; my quick instrument shows the sensitivity. This is actually an important honest finding for the design: the \"control\" formula is only reproducible under a precise task model (W separate vs folded, AFAB vs 1F1B ordering, whether the last stage's forwards precede its backwards). So G1 should be reformulated as: match a *reference implementation* of the simulator with cross-validated analytic under a fixed declared task convention, plus reproducibility across conventions reported. I should report this honestly rather than claim G1 passes.\n\nI've spent a fair number of steps (used ~7 of 60). I should now check the interleaved bug (agg=0.9969 is clearly wrong — because for v=2 with unit→device mapping u%p, program per device interleaves units in a weird order, and my \"steady state\" loop per unit produces invalid ordering). Rather than debug deeply, I'll note the instrument needs the virtual-stage program order fixed (Megatron's interleaved order iterates over virtual chunks within each 1F1B iteration). Let me do a quick fix for interleaved: program for device s: for each 1F1B \"iteration\" k, iterate over virtual chunks c in 0..v-1 of that device. This matters for the design's credibility but it's an instrument detail. Let me do one quick implementation to see if it matches, since G1 for interleaved is one of the researcher-approved controls.\n\nTime/step budget is fine. Let me implement a cleaner canonical 1F1B for interleaved (v virtual chunks per device, chunk order forward ascending, backward descending, as in Megatron).\n\nSimpler: define units by global position: unit index u, device = u % p, virtual chunk c = u // p. For each device, tasks: F(i,u) for u in that device. Canonical interleaved 1F1B (Megatron): num_warmup = (P-1-u) forward passes at the beginning of that unit... Actually Megatron interleaved schedules per virtual model chunk with warmup = p-1 for chunk 0 etc. Honestly, implementing Megatron's exact interleaved schedule is a rabbit hole. Given this is a design-only deliverable, I'll fix the ordering with a reasonable canonical definition and report that exact reproduction of the textbook interleaved formula requires the canonical chunk order, verified to within tolerance, else G1 is limited to AFAB/1F1B. Let me do one attempt with a \"global step\" formulation:\n\nCanonical interleaved 1F1B order per device s: \nwarmup phase: for k in range(W_s): for c in range(v): F(k, u(s,c))\nsteady: for i in range(W_s, m): for c in range(v): F(i,u(s,c)) ; then for c in reversed: B(i,u(s,c))\ncooldown: for i in range(W_s): for c in reversed(range(v)): B(i, u(s,c))\nwith W_s = P-1-s? For interleaved, warmup microbatches W = (P-1-s')/v where s' = position... In Megatron: num_warmup_microbatches = min(m, (pp_size - pp_rank - 1) + (total-1)*pp_size) for the first virtual chunk... it's per virtual chunk. The number of warmup microbatches is the same for all chunks of a device: (p - rank - 1) + (v-1)*p = P - 1 - rank - p + ... Let me just use W = min(m, (p-1-rank) + (v-1)*p) which is the Megatron formula: num_warmup_microbatches = min(m, (pp_size - rank - 1) + (V-1)*pp_size). Let me try that with the ordering above and see if agg approaches (p-1)/(vm+p-1).\n\nLet me implement quickly and test. If it matches within a few %, good; if not, I report honestly that G1 is validated only for the single-chunk case in this instrument, and that the interleaved reference must come from the library's own schedule trace.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cat > /workspace/design/sched_sim.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"CPU-only schedule simulator -- DESIGN INSTRUMENT ONLY (no GPU; validates the measurement\nconvention and the G1 control). NOT the experiment that answers the question.\n\nTASK CONVENTION (declared, this is what makes every number in this design reproducible):\n  per (microbatch i, pipeline unit u): F = forward (f), B = backward/activation-grad (b),\n  W = weight-grad (w). Unit u in [0,p*v), device(u)=u%p, virtual chunk c(u)=u//p.\n  Textbook formula (p-1)/(m+p-1) is reproduced ONLY under the convention t_layer = f+b\n  (no separate W, comm=0). We therefore report both:\n     T_work = m*(f+b+w)         (work per device)\n     bubble = 1 - sum(busy)/(p*T_step)\nG1 control is run with w=0, b=f  -> must equal (p-1)/(m+p-1) exactly for AFAB/1F1B,\nand (p-1)/(v*m+p-1) for interleaved-1F1B.\nDeps: F(i,u) <- F(i,u-1) ; B(i,u) <- F(i,u), B(i,u+1) ; W(i,u) <- B(i,u)\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\ndef _prog_1f1b(p, m, v, policy):\n    \"\"\"Megatron-canonical program. v=1: 1F1B. v>1: interleaved-1F1B (all chunks of a\n    microbatch forward ascending, backward descending, per 1F1B slot).\"\"\"\n    P = p * v\n    prog = [[] for _ in range(p)]\n    for s in range(p):\n        units = [s + c * p for c in range(v)]          # chunk order forward: ascending c\n        W = m if policy == \"afab\" else min(m, (P - 1 - s * v) // v + (v - 1) if v > 1 else min(m, p - 1 - s))\n        if policy == \"afab\":\n            seq = [(\"F\", i, u) for u in units for i in range(m)]\n            seq = [(\"F\", i, u) for i in range(m) for u in units]\n            seq += [(\"B\", i, u) for i in range(m) for u in reversed(units)]\n            seq += [(\"W\", i, u) for i in range(m) for u in units]\n        else:\n            W = min(m, (p - 1 - s) * v) if v > 1 else min(m, p - 1 - s)\n            seq = [(\"F\", i, u) for i in range(W) for u in units]\n            for i in range(W, m):\n                seq += [(\"F\", i, u) for u in units]\n                seq += [(\"B\", i, u) for u in reversed(units)]\n                seq += [(\"W\", i, u) for u in units]\n            for i in range(W):\n                seq += [(\"B\", i, u) for u in reversed(units)]\n                seq += [(\"W\", i, u) for u in units]\n        prog[s] = seq\n    return prog\n\ndef _prog_zb2p(p, m, v, warm_frac):\n    \"\"\"ZB(2p)-like program, written from the *schedule-graph* rule, not from any CLI flag:\n    warmup depth limited by max_pending_backward = 2p; weight-grads (W) of the first\n    microbatches are deferred and packed into the idle slots ('hitchhiked').\"\"\"\n    P = p * v\n    limit = 2 * p\n    prog = [[] for _ in range(p)]\n    for s in range(p):\n        units = [s + c * p for c in range(v)]\n        W = min(m, max(0, min(limit, p - 1 - s)))\n        seq = [(\"F\", i, u) for i in range(W) for u in units]\n        for i in range(W, m):\n            seq += [(\"F\", i, u) for u in units, ] if False else [(\"F\", i, u) for u in units]\n            seq += [(\"B\", i, u) for u in reversed(units)]\n        for i in range(W):\n            seq += [(\"B\", i, u) for u in reversed(units)]\n        seq += [(\"W\", i, u) for i in range(m) for u in units]   # deferred weight grads\n        prog[s] = seq\n    return prog\n\ndef simulate(p, m, f, b, w=0.0, v=1, policy=\"1f1b\", stage_scale=None, comm=0.0):\n    P = p * v\n    dev = lambda u: u % p\n    dur = {\"F\": f / v, \"B\": b / v, \"W\": w / v}\n    scale = (lambda u: 1.0) if stage_scale is None else stage_scale\n    prog = (_prog_zb2p(p, m, v, None) if policy == \"zb2p\" else _prog_1f1b(p, m, v, policy))\n    task = {}; start = {}\n    for s in range(p):\n        for t in prog[s]:\n            task[t] = (s, dur[t[0]] * scale(t[2]))\n            start[t] = 0.0\n    edges = {}\n    for s in range(p):\n        for a, c in zip(prog[s], prog[s][1:]):\n            edges.setdefault(a, []).append(c)\n    for (k, i, u) in task:\n        if k == \"F\" and u > 0: edges.setdefault((\"F\", i, u - 1), []).append((k, i, u))\n        if k == \"B\":\n            edges.setdefault((\"F\", i, u), []).append((k, i, u))\n            if u < P - 1: edges.setdefault((\"B\", i, u + 1), []).append((k, i, u))\n        if k == \"W\": edges.setdefault((\"B\", i, u), []).append((k, i, u))\n    E = lambda t: start[t] + task[t][1]\n    for _ in range(6 * len(task) + 16):\n        ch = False\n        for t in list(task):\n            for nx in edges.get(t, ()):\n                if E(t) > start[nx]: start[nx] = E(t); ch = True\n        if not ch: break\n    T = max(E(t) for t in task)\n    bydev = {s: [] for s in range(p)}\n    for t, (s, d) in task.items(): bydev[s].append((start[t], E(t)))\n    rows = []\n    for s in range(p):\n        tl = sorted(bydev[s]); busy = sum(e - a for a, e in tl)\n        intra = sum(tl[j+1][0] - tl[j][1] for j in range(len(tl) - 1))\n        rows.append(dict(stage=s, busy=busy, idle=T - busy, bubble=(T - busy) / T,\n                         pre=tl[0][0], intra=intra, post=T - tl[-1][1]))\n    return dict(T=T, agg=1 - sum(r[\"busy\"] for r in rows) / (p * T), per_stage=rows)\n\ndef memory_depth(p, m, v=1, policy=\"1f1b\", limit=None):\n    \"\"\"Peak stored-activation slots per device = max #microbatches forward-but-not-backward.\"\"\"\n    P = p * v\n    prog = (_prog_zb2p(p, m, v, None) if policy == \"zb2p\" else _prog_1f1b(p, m, v, policy))\n    peak = 0\n    for s in range(p):\n        held = 0; hi = 0\n        for k, i, u in prog[s]:\n            if k == \"F\": held += 1; hi = max(hi, held)\n            elif k == \"B\": held -= 1\n        peak = max(peak, hi)\n    return peak\nPY\ncd /workspace/design && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom sched_sim import simulate, memory_depth\nprint(\"== G1 control: w=0, b=f=1 -> must match textbook ==\")\nbad=[]\nfor p in (2,4,8):\n    for m in (p,2*p,4*p,8*p,16*p):\n        for pol,ana in ((\"afab\",(p-1)/(m+p-1)), (\"1f1b\",(p-1)/(m+p-1))):\n            r=simulate(p,m,1,1,0,policy=pol)\n            if abs(r['agg']-ana)>1e-9: bad.append((p,m,pol,round(r['agg'],5),round(ana,5)))\nprint(\"  AFAB/1F1B mismatches:\", bad or \"NONE (exact match)\")\nr=simulate(4,16,1,1,0,v=2,policy=\"1f1b\"); print(\"  interleaved v=2 p=4 m=16: sim=%.5f analytic=%.5f\"%(r['agg'],3/(2*16+3)))\nr=simulate(8,64,1,1,0,v=4,policy=\"1f1b\"); print(\"  interleaved v=4 p=8 m=64: sim=%.5f analytic=%.5f\"%(r['agg'],7/(4*64+7)))\nprint(\"== general ratio (b != f), textbook does not apply: report measured ==\")\nfor (f,b) in ((1,1),(1,2),(1,3)):\n    r=simulate(8,64,f,b,0.5,policy=\"1f1b\"); print(f\"  p=8 m=64 f={f} b={b} w=0.5: T={r['T']:.2f} agg={r['agg']:.4f}\")\nprint(\"== drain vs intra decomposition (p=8,m=64,f=1,b=2,w=1, 1f1b) ==\")\nr=simulate(8,64,1,2,1,policy=\"1f1b\")\nfor row in r['per_stage']: print(\"   stage %d idle=%.2f pre=%.2f intra=%.2f drain(post)=%.2f\"%(row['stage'],row['idle'],row['pre'],row['intra'],row['post']))\nprint(\"== zb2p-like variant (structural, illustrative of instrument, NOT a result) ==\")\nfor pol in (\"1f1b\",\"zb2p\"):\n    r=simulate(8,64,1,1,1,policy=pol); md=memory_depth(8,64,policy=pol)\n    print(f\"  {pol:5s} T={r['T']:.2f} agg_bubble={r['agg']:.4f} peak_act_slots={md}\")\nPY", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99fc156b1f63b9b9", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-99fc156b1f63b9b9", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /workspace/design/sched_sim.py <<'PY'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"CPU-only schedule simulator -- DESIGN INSTRUMENT ONLY (no GPU; validates the measurement\\nconvention and the G1 control). NOT the experiment that answers the question.\\n\\nTASK CONVENTION (declared, this is what makes every number in this design reproducible):\\n  per (microbatch i, pipeline unit u): F = forward (f), B = backward/activation-grad (b),\\n  W = weight-grad (w). Unit u in [0,p*v), device(u)=u%p, virtual chunk c(u)=u//p.\\n  Textbook f