{"id": "ce4d8cf2-8df9-46b8-84cf-868615bc2bbb", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:15:18.701852", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "67ac7f22-196d-4bd9-a8d9-a28bb7d160c3", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "El fixpoint tipo Bellman-Ford escala mal en Python. Lo cambio a orden topológico (Kahn), que es lineal."}], "reasoning_content": "The Bellman-Ford fixpoint is O(V*E) with E ~ tasks*3, tasks ~ 3*p*m*v*... for p=8,m=128,v=1: 3*8*128 = 3072 tasks; iterations up to 6*3072 = 18k passes × 3072 tasks × edges ≈ 10^8 → too slow in Python. Need topological order instead. Let me implement proper Kahn topological sort, and limit sizes. Let me rewrite with topo order.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cd /workspace/design && python3 - <<'PY'\ns=open('sched_sim.py').read()\nold = \"\"\"    E = lambda t: start[t] + task[t][1]\n    for _ in range(6 * len(task) + 16):\n        ch = False\n        for t in list(task):\n            for nx in edges.get(t, ()):\n                if E(t) > start[nx]: start[nx] = E(t); ch = True\n        if not ch: break\n    T = max(E(t) for t in task)\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    # exact ASAP via topological order (Kahn) over {program edges, dependency edges}\n    succ = {t: [] for t in task}\n    indeg = {t: 0 for t in task}\n    for a, ns in edges.items():\n        for c in ns:\n            succ[a].append(c); indeg[c] += 1\n    from collections import deque\n    q = deque(t for t in task if indeg[t] == 0); topo = []\n    while q:\n        t = q.popleft(); topo.append(t)\n        for c in succ[t]:\n            indeg[c] -= 1\n            if indeg[c] == 0: q.append(c)\n    assert len(topo) == len(task), \"cycle in schedule graph (program+deps)\"\n    E = lambda t: start[t] + task[t][1]\n    for t in topo:\n        for nx in succ[t]:\n            if E(t) > start[nx]: start[nx] = E(t)\n    T = max(E(t) for t in task)\"\"\"\nassert old in s\nopen('sched_sim.py','w').write(s.replace(old,new))\npri