 that code base. Fallback artifact:\\n       the schedule-graph simulator + generator becomes the explicit substitute, and any statement is\\n       restricted to \\\"a ZB(2p)-defined schedule graph\\\", never to \\\"Megatron's ZB-2p\\\".\\nIn all branches, evidence of activation is the executed-schedule fingerprint (G3), never the flag name.\\nNegative control retained: force fallback to 1F1B and confirm the fingerprint changes.\\n\\n## 1. (a) Operational definition + pre-registered threshold\\nNotation: p pipeline stages, m microbatches, v virtual chunks/stage, one GPU per stage.\\nTask model per (microbatch i, unit u): F (f, forward), B (b, activation grad), W (w, weight grad).\\nDeclared convention (makes every number reproducible): comm accounted separately; W is a task;\\n\\\"step\\\" = one optimizer iteration excluding initial NCCL/model warmup; T_step = wall time of the step.\\n\\n  N1 structural bubble (schedule graph, no hardware):\\n       B1 = 1 - m*(f+b+w) / (p * T_sched)\\n  N2 device bubble (wall-clock, from traces; the headline number):\\n       busy_s = SUM duration of model-compute kernels/regions on device s inside [t0,t_step]\\n                (excludes NCCL p2p waits, optimizer, allocator, profiler overhead)\\n       B2_mean = 1 - (SUM_s busy_s)/(p*T_step);  B2_max = max_s (1 - busy_s/T_step)\\n  N3 effective bubble (does it matter?):\\n       B3 = (T_step - T_ideal)/T_step,  T_ideal = m*(f~+b~+w~)/p with f~,b~,w~ measured standalone\\n       on the same hardware/shapes (single-microbatch, no pipeline).\\n\\n  \\\"Near-zero\\\" = pre-registered joint criterion at the operating point P0op = (p=8, m=8p,\\n  balanced stages, recompute OFF, overlap ON, no OOM):\\n       B2_mean <= 2.0%  AND  B2_max <= 5.0%  AND  B3 <= 5.0%\\n  plus a scaling clause: B2_mean(m) monotone decreasing and <= 2.0% for every m >= 8p.\\n  Threshold fixed here, before any measurement; not tunable afterwards. If N1 ~ 0 but N2/N3 fail,\\n  the verdict is \\\"structural only / not confirmed in practice\\\", never \\\"yes\\\".\\n\\n## 2. (b) Condition matrix\\nCore tier (single node, 1 GPU/stage, TP=1, DP=1, no multi-node):\\n  p in {2,4,8}; m in {p,2p,4p,8p}; v=1 for main arms (v=2 only for the interleaved baseline)\\n  arms: ZB-2p (or P0-equivalent), 1F1B, interleaved-1F1B v=2, AFAB (memory-cost reference, p<=4, m in {p,2p})\\n  load balance: {balanced, +25% single mid-stage, +25% last stage}\\n  b/f ratio: as-measured (reported per model), plus one forced recompute variant\\n  seeds/reps: 3 repetitions per cell, 5 measured steps each after >=3 discarded warmup steps\\nExtension (optional, out of core): p=16 across 2 nodes; v in {2,4}; comm-overlap OFF; b/f by\\n  choosing layer shapes; GPUs/stage>1 (TP) \\u2014 declared secondary because TP confounds stage time.\\n\\n## 3. (c) Controls and baselines\\n  G1 instrument control (CPU): simulator reproduces AFAB/1F1B analytic bubble (p-1)/(m+p-1) exactly\\n     under the declared convention (w=0, b=f, comm=0). VERIFIED here: 40/40 exact for p in {2,4,8,16},\\n     m in {p..16p}. NOT satisfied by my reimplementation for interleaved-1F1B -> so for interleaved the\\n     control is \\\"instrument == library-emitted schedule\\\", not the textbook (p-1)/(vm+p-1).\\n  G2 calibration control (GPU): measured 1F1B B2 must reproduce its N1 value within +/-1 pp at the\\n     same (p,m) using a GENERAL formula, because the textbook form assumes equal task times.\\n     General rule used: no closed form is asserted for b != f or w>0; instead N1 from the simulator,\\n     fed with f,b,w measured on that hardware, is the reference. Textbook forms are cited only for\\n     the equal-time special case. ZB-variant bubble formulas remain TO-VERIFY (U5) and are NOT\\n     controls.\\n  G3 activation fingerprint: parsed-args dump + scheduler class/branch logged + schedule invariants\\n     (max concurrently-pending backward == 2p, activation-slot depth, F/B interleaving pattern in the\\n     trace) + negative control forcing 1F1B showing the fingerprint changes.\\n  Negative control (silent fallback): same binary/flags with ZB disabled -> fingerprint must differ.\\n  Determinism controls: fixed seeds/dataset order, pinned clocks, no other GPU tenants, identical\\n  build/commit recorded per run.\\n\\n## 4. (d) Instruments and measurement protocol\\n  1. Schedule simulator (CPU-only DESIGN ARTIFACT, already prototyped here, 40/40 G1 exact, 10 ms per\\n     config): fixes the task-graph convention, computes N1 and the pre/intra/post-drain split.\\n     Unit tests: G1 identities; peak-activation-slot depth vs warmup depth; DAG acyclicity assertion.\\n     Explicitly NOT the experiment: it cannot answer the question about real GPUs.\\n  2. Trace instrumentation: torch.profiler (kineto) chrome-trace per rank over 5 steps, with\\n     record_function(\\\"fwd_mb{i}\\\"/\\\"bwd_mb{i}\\\"/\\\"wgrad_mb{i}\\\") and a per-step barrier; step window bounded\\n     by a logged collective so all ranks share one [t0,t_step].\\n  3. Parser: deterministic script -> per-rank busy_s, idle decomposition into pre-idle (pipeline fill),\\n     intra-step gaps, and POST-idle (final drain), reported separately; NCCL p2p/recv kernels excluded\\n     from busy but reported as a separate wait series. Validated on synthetic traces whose busy/idle\\n     intervals are known by construction (unit test), reusing the simulator's schedule as ground truth.\\n  4. Cross-check: nsys (Nsight Systems) with Megatron --profile-step-start/end where available, to\\n     confirm kernel-level busy attribution; library timers (elapsed time per iteration,\\n     forward/backward-compute, MFU) give B3 and throughput.\\n  5. Memory as a first-class outcome: torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated per rank, peak-activation-slot\\n     count, recompute-triggered events, OOM/fallback counts (OOM is a recorded outcome, not a dropped run).\\n  Procedure: identical commit/build per arm; run order randomized within cell; 3 reps; log every flag.\\n\\n## 5. (e) Analysis plan and decision rule\\n  Report per cell: B1 (sim), B2_mean, B2_max, B3, pre/intra/drain idle (absolute ms and % of T_step),\\n  peak memory ratio vs 1F1B, OOM count, throughput tokens/s, with median +/- IQR over reps.\\n  Decomposition rule: drain idle is reported separately from intra-step idle; a claim of near-zero\\n  steady-state bubble must hold on intra-step idle specifically, because at large m the final drain can\\n  dominate the aggregate and mask it (illustrated by the instrument's per-stage drain table).\\n  Primary comparison: ZB-2p vs 1F1B and vs interleaved-1F1B v=2 at equal (p,m); throughput\\n  improvement with bootstrap CI over reps; equivalence/tie declared if CI covers 0.\\n  DECISION RULE (pre-registered):\\n    YES        : G1..G3 pass, Sec.1 threshold met at P0op and for all m>=8p, with no OOM and\\n                 no recompute triggered, AND measured step time <= interleaved-1F1B.\\n    YES-AT-COST: bubble criterion met but peak activation memory > 1F1B and/or recompute triggered\\n                 and/or step time not better than interleaved-1F1B -> reported as\\n                 \\\"near-zero bubble, paid in memory / not in throughput\\\".\\n    NO         : B2_mean > 5% or B2_max > 10% or B3 > 10% at P0op, or OOM, or drain-dominated idle\\n                 keeps B2_mean above the 2% band for every m tested.\\n    CONDITIONAL: threshold met only in a sub-region of (p,m,balance) -> report the region and the\\n                 boundary m at which B2_mean crosses 2%/5%.\\n    NOT EVALUABLE: P0 branch (iii) (no ZB-2p in the code base) or G3 fails (fingerprint says the run\\n                 executed a non-ZB schedule).\\n  Sensitivity: one axis at a time (m, p, imbalance, recompute) around P0op; no post-hoc threshold moves.\\n\\n## 6. (f) Feasibility and cost (labelled)\\n  Executable here (CPU-only, 224 cores, no GPU): Sec.0 discovery greps against a provided checkout;\\n  simulator + unit tests (built and G1-validated here); parser validation on synthetic traces;\\n  full analysis pipeline code. NOT executable here: anything requiring CUDA.\\n  CORE tier cost \\u2014 ESTIMATION only, order of magnitude (no measurement, no benchmark performed):\\n    ~12 (p,m) cells x 3 main arms x 3 balance x 3 reps ~ 216 runs + small AFAB subset;\\n    per run ~3-5 min (build-free: startup + warmup + 5 profiled steps);\\n    1 GPU/stage -> ~70 GPU-hours ~ 9 h wall on one 8-GPU node => order 1e2 GPU-h, <1 node-day.\\n  FULL/extension tier: + p=16 (2 nodes), v in {2,4}, overlap on/off, forced b/f variants =>\\n    order 1e3 GPU-h, multi-day, multi-node scheduler risk.\\n  What falls away if the budget is smaller (declared degradation):\\n    budget < ~10 GPU-h -> p={4} only, m in {4p,8p}, 1 balance level, 2 reps: tests only the headline\\n      claim at one p, cannot separate imbalance or scaling effects;\\n    no profiler support -> keep timers-based B3 + library schedule dump, drop N2 kernel-level split;\\n    single GPU only -> run p=2 with 1 GPU emulating stages sequentially (B1/B3 partial; B2 invalid);\\n    no second node -> drop p=16 and all multi-node claims (they become explicit limitations);\\n    no nsys -> B2 relies on torch.profiler alone, stated as a single-instrument limitation.\\n\\n## 7. Assumptions vs open items\\nASSUMPTIONS (mine, not source-backed): repo is Megatron-LM/Core with a PP scheduler; \\\"ZB-2p\\\" means\\n  max-pending-backward beta=2p; torch.profiler + timers are the available instruments; 1 GPU/stage with\\n  TP=DP=1 is representative for attribution; task times stationary across microbatches; the 2%/5%\\n  thresholds and the (p,m) grid are my pre-registered choices; random weights are acceptable for\\n  timing; per-run cost estimate above is an ESTIMATION.\\nOPEN / UNCERTAIN: ZB-2p may be absent or differently activated (P0 branch iii); no GPU/driver here, so\\n  the multi-GPU profiling cannot be run in this environment (nothing has been run); external compute\\n  budget unknown (U3) \\u2014 hence the two-tier design; no datasets/checkpoints, limiting external validity;\\n  ZB bubble/memory formulas cited from the paper remain to-verify (U5) and are excluded from controls;\\n  whether ZB-2p is emitted by an automatic schedule generator or is a hand-written path (changes G3).\\nMD\\nwc -l /workspace/design/DESIGN.md && python3 -c \\\"import pathlib;print('files:',[p.name for p in pathlib.Path('/workspace/design').iterdir()])\\\"\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.115, \"output\": \"145 /workspace/design/DESIGN.md\\nfiles: ['sched_sim.py', '__pycache__', 'DESIGN.md']\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "e85ba14c-626e-4ede-a27e-e50e2464016f", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
{"id": "4abbba17-8071-400a-b310-a990674db04c", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:22:09.667457", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "c1b15558-3614-4efb-9686-cd8aab337f30", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Design doc written. Let me do a final quick sanity check that the simulator file still imports and G1 holds (already verified). Also add a small unit-test file? Optional; the researcher asked for unit tests as part of the design of the artifact. I've demonstrated the G1 test inline. Let me add a tiny test file quickly to be complete, run it, then hand off result.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cat > /workspace/design/test_sched_sim.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Unit tests for the design instrument (G1 control + decomposition bookkeeping).\"\"\"\nimport unittest\nfrom sched_sim import simulate, program, peak_activation_slots\n\nclass T(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_g1_afab_1f1b_textbook(self):\n        for p in (2, 4, 8, 16):\n            for k in (1, 2, 4, 8, 16):\n                m = k * p; a = (p - 1) / (m + p - 1)\n                for pol in (\"afab\", \"1f1b\"):\n                    self.assertAlmostEqual(simulate(p, m, 1, 1, 0, policy=pol)[\"agg\"], a, places=12)\n    def test_no_cycles_and_task_counts(self):\n        for pol in (\"afab\", \"1f1b\", \"zb2p\"):\n            for p in (2, 4, 8):\n                pr = program(p, 3 * p, policy=pol)\n                self.assertEqual(sum(len(x) for x in pr), 3 * p * p * 3)   # m*p tasks x {F,B,W}\n    def test_idle_decomposition_sums_to_idle(self):\n        r = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1)\n        for row in r[\"per_stage\"]:\n            self.assertAlmostEqual(row[\"pre\"] + row[\"intra\"] + row[\"post\"], row[\"idle\"], places=9)\n            self.assertGreaterEqual(row[\"post\"], 0); self.assertGreaterEqual(row[\"intra\"], 0)\n    def test_drain_is_monotone_in_stage_for_balanced_1f1b(self):\n        r = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1)\n        posts = [x[\"post\"] for x in r[\"per_stage\"]]\n        self.assertEqual(posts, sorted(posts))\n    def test_afab_memory_depth_is_m(self):\n        self.assertEqual(peak_activation_slots(4, 16, policy=\"afab\"), 16)\n        self.assertLess(peak_activation_slots(4, 16, policy=\"1f1b\"), 16)\n    def test_imbalance_increases_bubble(self):\n        b = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1)[\"agg\"]\n        i = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1, imbalance=lambda u: 1.25 if u == 4 else 1.0)[\"agg\"]\n        self.assertGreater(i, b)\nPY\ncd /workspace/design && rm -rf __pycache__ && python3 -m unittest -v test_sched_sim 2>&1 | tail -15", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-93cb18f99f618534", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-93cb18f99f618534", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /workspace/design/test_sched_sim.py <<'PY'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Unit tests for the design instrument (G1 control + decomposition bookkeeping).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport unittest\\nfrom sched_sim import simulate, program, peak_activation_slots\\n\\nclass T(unittest.TestCase):\\n    def test_g1_afab_1f1b_textbook(self):\\n        for p in (2, 4, 8, 16):\\n            for k in (1, 2, 4, 8, 16):\\n                m = k * p; a = (p - 1) / (m + p - 1)\\n                for pol in (\\\"afab\\\", \\\"1f1b\\\"):\\n                    self.assertAlmostEqual(simulate(p, m, 1, 1, 0, policy=pol)[\\\"agg\\\"], a, places=12)\\n    def test_no_cycles_and_task_counts(self):\\n        for pol in (\\\"afab\\\", \\\"1f1b\\\", \\\"zb2p\\\"):\\n            for p in (2, 4, 8):\\n                pr = program(p, 3 * p, policy=pol)\\n                self.assertEqual(sum(len(x) for x in pr), 3 * p * p * 3)   # m*p tasks x {F,B,W}\\n    def test_idle_decomposition_sums_to_idle(self):\\n        r = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1)\\n        for row in r[\\\"per_stage\\\"]:\\n            self.assertAlmostEqual(row[\\\"pre\\\"] + row[\\\"intra\\\"] + row[\\\"post\\\"], row[\\\"idle\\\"], places=9)\\n            self.assertGreaterEqual(row[\\\"post\\\"], 0); self.assertGreaterEqual(row[\\\"intra\\\"], 0)\\n    def test_drain_is_monotone_in_stage_for_balanced_1f1b(self):\\n        r = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1)\\n        posts = [x[\\\"post\\\"] for x in r[\\\"per_stage\\\"]]\\n        self.assertEqual(posts, sorted(posts))\\n    def test_afab_memory_depth_is_m(self):\\n        self.assertEqual(peak_activation_slots(4, 16, policy=\\\"afab\\\"), 16)\\n        self.assertLess(peak_activation_slots(4, 16, policy=\\\"1f1b\\\"), 16)\\n    def test_imbalance_increases_bubble(self):\\n        b = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1)[\\\"agg\\\"]\\n        i = simulate(8, 64, 1, 2, 1, imbalance=lambda u: 1.25 if u == 4 else 1.0)[\\\"agg\\\"]\\n        self.assertGreater(i, b)\\nPY\\ncd /workspace/design && rm -rf __pycache__ && python3 -m unittest -v test_sched_sim 2>&1 | tail -15\", \"summary\": \"Add and run unit tests for the design instrument\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-ff7cd017-a2c6-43da-b00a-f2a1dd5f30ce", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Add and run unit tests for the design instrument", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
